# Fetched external payloads — Agmarknet prices, Open-Meteo weather, ERA5 hazard
# climatology. **Committed on purpose** (14.7 MB): NFR-303 requires the demo to run with the
# network disabled, and a fixture bundle that only exists on the machine that fetched it is
# not a fixture bundle. `git clone && make seed` has to work on a train.
#
# Re-fetching is possible but not required: seed/fetch_agmarknet.py, fetch_weather.py and
# fetch_climatology.py all write here, and the Agmarknet endpoint is undocumented and may
# stop working — which is precisely why the responses are kept rather than the ability to
# ask for them again.

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Generated contracts (regenerated from OpenAPI)
packages/contracts/src/generated/

# Logs
*.log

# Per-clone fetch log; append-only and conflicts on every merge.
# The shared state that matters is seed/generated/fetch_state.json, which IS tracked.
seed/generated/fetch_log.jsonl

# The ONNX sentence encoder, fetched by `make embed-model`. NOT committed, unlike the data
# fixtures above: it is ~120 MB of redistributable model weights that add nothing to the
# audit trail, and retrieval degrades to Postgres full-text search without it, so a clone
# that never runs the target still works offline.
apps/api/models/
